    <node id="main::run_deep_learning">
      <data key="d0">main::run_deep_learning</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">run_deep_learning(results_dir) is a small orchestration function that launches the project’s deep learning training pipeline. It prints a start message, imports DLTrainer from src.deep_learning.trainer, creates a DLTrainer instance, and calls its train(results_dir) method. After training completes it prints a success message and reports the provided results_dir where outputs are saved. The function has no return value and may raise exceptions if the import or training step fails.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faa1c94bade9df8eda3dfcb844c497b</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_physics_informed">
      <data key="d0">main::run_physics_informed</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">A small top-level function that launches a Physics-Informed Neural Network (PINN) training run. It prints a start message, imports PINNTrainer from src.physics_informed.trainer, instantiates the trainer, calls trainer.train(results_dir) to perform the training (using the provided results_dir as the output location), and then prints completion and the results directory. The function has no return value and performs I/O via printing and whatever the trainer.train method does (e.g., saving files); it may raise errors from the import or training process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faa1c94bade9df8eda3dfcb844c497b</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::main">
      <data key="d0">main::main</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Entry-point function for the Magnetic Field Predictor script. It parses a required command-line option --method (choices: 'dl' or 'pinn'), creates a timestamped results directory named results/&amp;lt;TIMESTAMP&amp;gt;_&amp;lt;METHOD&amp;gt;, configures logging to both a training.log file in that directory and the console, prints the results path, and then dispatches to either run_deep_learning(results_dir) or run_physics_informed(results_dir) depending on the chosen method. After the selected routine finishes it prints completion messages. The function performs filesystem and logging side effects and does not return a value.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9faa1c94bade9df8eda3dfcb844c497b</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
