    <node id="main::load_config">
      <data key="d0">main::load_config</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Reads a YAML configuration file at the given path and returns the parsed configuration as a Python object. The function opens the file, calls yaml.safe_load on its contents, and returns the resulting data structure (propagating any I/O or YAML parsing exceptions).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-004f8b9900d46ba80c25407fb2cb335a</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_attention_model">
      <data key="d0">main::run_attention_model</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Starts and runs a full training pipeline for an Attention-based model. Given a configuration dict, a data path and a data type, it: creates a results directory and logging locations, updates the config with tensorboard/log dirs, loads the dataset via DataLoader and prints dataset info, constructs an AttentionModel from model settings in the config, initializes an AttentionTrainer with the model and data loader, runs training and evaluation, prints the final test loss, optionally saves the trained model to the results folder, and returns the trained model object plus the results directory path. The function also emits progress/info messages to stdout and writes logs to the created log directory.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-004f8b9900d46ba80c25407fb2cb335a</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::create_results_directory">
      <data key="d0">main::create_results_directory</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Creates a timestamped results directory under a top-level "results" folder. It builds a directory name using the current local datetime formatted as YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS plus the provided model_type and data_type ("&amp;lt;timestamp&amp;gt;_&amp;lt;model_type&amp;gt;_&amp;lt;data_type&amp;gt;"), ensures the directory (and any missing parent directories) exists, and returns a pathlib.Path to that directory. The call is idempotent (exist_ok=True).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-004f8b9900d46ba80c25407fb2cb335a</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::setup_logging">
      <data key="d0">main::setup_logging</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Ensures the given log_dir exists, creates a timestamped log file named training_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log inside it, and configures Python logging to INFO level with a timestamped message format. Logging is directed both to the created file (via logging.FileHandler) and to the console (via logging.StreamHandler). The function returns the Path to the created log file.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-004f8b9900d46ba80c25407fb2cb335a</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_rnn_model">
      <data key="d0">main::run_rnn_model</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Runs end-to-end training and evaluation of an RNN using the provided configuration and dataset. Specifically, it: creates a results directory and sets up logging; updates the config with log/tensorboard paths; initializes a DataLoader for the specified data_path and data_type and prints dataset info; constructs an RNNModel from the config and wraps it with an RNNTrainer; trains the model and evaluates it to produce a test loss; optionally saves the trained model (controlled by config['logging']['save_model'], default True); prints status messages throughout. It returns the trained model instance and the path to the results directory. The function also mutates the config by inserting log directory paths and produces side effects (files/logs saved to disk).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-004f8b9900d46ba80c25407fb2cb335a</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_q_learning">
      <data key="d0">main::run_q_learning</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Starts and runs a Q-Learning optimization session. Given an environment name (string), a configuration object, and a results directory path, the function: (1) prints a start message; (2) instantiates the appropriate environment class (SynRMEnvironment for "synrm", CCoreEnvironment for "ccore"); (3) raises ValueError for unknown environment names; (4) creates a QLearningTrainer with the chosen environment and config; (5) runs trainer.train(results_dir); and (6) prints completion and results-directory messages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d242b29aca3f07293327977b1717c97e</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_comparison">
      <data key="d0">main::run_comparison</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Orchestrates a comparison run between two optimization methods (Q-Learning and a Genetic Algorithm) across two environments. It prints a start message, then for each environment in ["synrm", "ccore"] it initializes results[env_name] = {} and iterates over methods ["ql", "ga"]. For method "ql" it calls run_q_learning(env_name, config, results_dir / f"{env_name}_ql"); for "ga" it calls run_genetic_algorithm(env_name, config, results_dir / f"{env_name}_ga"). After running all combinations it prints completion messages and the results directory. Notes: the function has no return value, relies on external globals/functions (results, run_q_learning, run_genetic_algorithm), and uses the provided config and results_dir to dispatch each experiment into a per-environment/method subpath.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d242b29aca3f07293327977b1717c97e</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_genetic_algorithm">
      <data key="d0">main::run_genetic_algorithm</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Function run_genetic_algorithm(environment_name, config, results_dir): orchestrates a Genetic Algorithm optimization run. It prints a start message, selects and instantiates an environment object based on the case-insensitive environment_name ('synrm' -&amp;gt; SynRMEnvironment, 'ccore' -&amp;gt; CCoreEnvironment), raises a ValueError for unknown names, constructs a GeneticAlgorithm with the chosen environment and provided config, runs its optimize method saving results to results_dir, and then prints completion and results-location messages.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d242b29aca3f07293327977b1717c97e</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="main::run_a2c">
      <data key="d0">main::run_a2c</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">run_a2c(config: dict, results_dir: Path) starts and runs an Advantage Actor-Critic (A2C) training session. It prints a start message, imports and instantiates src.a2c.trainer.A2CTrainer with the provided configuration and results directory, calls trainer.train() to execute training, then calls trainer.close(). After training it prints completion and summary statistics taken from the returned results dict (mean reward over the last 10 episodes, best reward, total episodes, and total training time). The function performs the training synchronously and does not return a value.</data>
