    <node id="agent::ProbabilityDistribution">
      <data key="d0">agent::ProbabilityDistribution</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">A small tf.keras.Model subclass that implements stochastic action sampling from logits. Its call(logits) uses tf.random.categorical(logits, 1) to draw one categorical sample per batch entry, then tf.squeeze(..., axis=-1) to return a 1-D tensor of sampled action indices (one int index per batch). The returned tensor contains integer class indices (tf.random.categorical produces int64). This is a non-differentiable sampler for converting action logits into sampled discrete actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-acd9afa9c91c00d207b7d3d68ec7f1f6</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="agent::A2CModel">
      <data key="d0">agent::A2CModel</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">A2CModel is a TensorFlow Keras model implementing the actor–critic (A2C) network used to produce policy logits and value estimates from image-like observations. It is constructed with a num_actions integer and a configuration dict that controls convolutional filters, kernel sizes, strides and hidden layer sizes. The network consists of two convolutional layers followed by a flattening layer, then two separate dense pathways: an actor_hidden dense that feeds a policy_head producing raw action logits (shape: [batch, num_actions]) and a critic_hidden dense that feeds a value_head producing scalar value estimates (shape: [batch, 1]). The model stores a ProbabilityDistribution helper used to sample actions from the returned logits and a logger. The call(inputs) method runs the forward pass and returns (policy_logits, value_estimates). The action_value(observation) convenience method accepts a single observation (adds a batch dimension if needed), runs prediction, samples an action via the ProbabilityDistribution, and returns the sampled action and the corresponding value (both squeezed to remove the extra batch dimension). The class inherits tf.keras.Model and is named 'a2c_model'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-acd9afa9c91c00d207b7d3d68ec7f1f6</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="agent::A2CAgent">
      <data key="d0">agent::A2CAgent</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">A2CAgent is an implementation of the Advantage Actor–Critic (A2C) agent that wraps a neural network policy/value model and provides action selection, return/advantage computation, and batched training. On construction it reads hyperparameters from a provided config (gamma, entropy_coefficient, value_coefficient, learning_rate), creates an A2CModel with the environment action dimension, and compiles it with RMSprop and two custom losses (policy and value). get_action(observation) queries the model for a sampled action and its value estimate. compute_returns_and_advantages(rewards, values, dones, next_value) computes discounted returns with episode termination handling and returns advantages as returns minus predicted values. train_step(observations, actions, returns, advantages) packages actions and advantages together and calls model.train_on_batch to update both policy and value heads, returning total, policy and value losses. The policy loss uses SparseCategoricalCrossentropy weighted by advantages plus an entropy term scaled by entropy_coefficient; the value loss is a mean-squared error scaled by value_coefficient. Utility methods save_model, load_model and get_model_summary persist and inspect model weights/architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-acd9afa9c91c00d207b7d3d68ec7f1f6</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
