      <data key="d2">I cannot see the class body in the provided snippet (the code is marked as "unknown"). From the name and the fact it subclasses tf.keras.Model, ProbabilityDistribution is the reinforcement‑learning agent component that represents an action probability distribution returned by the policy network. In typical A2C implementations this class acts as an abstract/utility wrapper around distribution parameters (e.g. logits or means/variances), provides methods to sample actions, compute log probabilities and entropies, and exposes a model call so distribution parameters can be produced or updated as part of the Keras graph. It is therefore used by the agent to (1) produce actions, (2) compute log_prob(action) for policy gradients, and (3) compute entropy for exploration/regularization. Without the implementation I cannot list the exact methods or fields.</data>
