      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">I cannot access the actual implementation from the provided metadata (the code is listed as "unknown" and only the file path/line is given). Based on the class name A2CAgent and common practice, this class is very likely an Advantage Actor‑Critic (A2C) agent implementation. Typical responsibilities you can expect in such a class are: managing the actor (policy) and critic (value) networks and their optimizers; interacting with the environment to select actions (often stochastic sampling from the policy) and collect rollouts; computing discounted returns and advantages; forming the combined A2C loss (policy loss, value loss, and entropy bonus) and applying gradient updates; storing and batching rollout data; and providing utility methods for saving/loading model checkpoints and switching between train/eval modes. If you provide the class source (or allow me to read the file), I can give a precise description tied to the actual implementation.</data>
