    <node id="agent::A2CModel::unknown">
      <data key="d0">agent::A2CModel::unknown</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">A2CModel is a custom TensorFlow Keras model class (subclassing tf.keras.Model) used by the repository’s Advantage Actor–Critic (A2C) agent. Although the implementation body is not provided here, its role is to implement the neural network used by the A2C algorithm — typically a shared feature extractor with two output heads: an actor head that produces policy logits or action probabilities and a critic head that predicts state values. In this codebase the class is expected to define the network layers, a call/forward method that returns the policy and value outputs (and possibly a sampled action or distribution), and helper functionality needed by the agent for computing action selection and value estimates during training and inference.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-acd9afa9c91c00d207b7d3d68ec7f1f6</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
