    <node id="attention_trainer::AttentionTrainer::load_model">
      <data key="d0">attention_trainer::AttentionTrainer::load_model</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Method of attention_trainer::AttentionTrainer that loads a saved Keras model from the given filepath. It calls tf.keras.models.load_model(filepath, custom_objects={'AttentionModel': AttentionModel}), stores the loaded model on self.model, prints a confirmation message with the filepath, and returns the loaded model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-968bf1bdb0ca466dad9c6091ddfd8491</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data_loader::DataLoader">
      <data key="d0">data_loader::DataLoader</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
      <data key="d2">DataLoader is a unified data-loading utility class for preparing batches used in efficiency or power-factor prediction. On initialization it configures file paths based on data_type ('efficiency' or 'powerfactor'), validates that the expected text directory and HDF5 file exist, reads sequence-length and input-dimension metadata from the text files, and attempts to start a MATLAB engine for optional visualization. Key attributes include data_path, text_path, hdf5_path, batch_size, dim_x/dim_y, inp_dim, names, seq_len (per-file lengths), seq_len_sorted and seq_len_order (sorted lengths and corresponding file indices), and an efficiency threshold (eff_threshold). The data_feed(index) method builds a batch of size batch_size by: reading sequential data from the text files (skipping the first two header lines), replacing negative values with zero, zero-padding sequences to the batch max length, and reading corresponding per-file input tensors from the HDF5 dataset '/DS_TrINP' (skipping the first HDF5 row). It returns X_inp (per-file inputs from HDF5), X (sequential features excluding the final column), Y (target values from the final column), and src_len (original sequence lengths). qualitative_measure uses the MATLAB engine to visualize a stacked [speed, torque, target, prediction, file_index] map (if MATLAB is available). quantitative_measure binarizes targets/predictions using eff_threshold, computes a confusion matrix, writes TN/FP/FN/TP to a file for the referenced sequence, and returns the matrix. get_data_info returns basic dataset metadata (type, file count, inp_dim, min/max/mean sequence length, and data_path). The class raises ValueError for an invalid data_type and FileNotFoundError if expected paths/files are missing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e758f46de7980f7b381133c2079910f4</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data_loader::DataLoader::unknown">
      <data key="d0">data_loader::DataLoader::unknown</data>
      <data key="d1">classs</data>
