    <node id="rnn_model::RNNModel::__init__">
      <data key="d0">rnn_model::RNNModel::__init__</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">Constructor for the RNNModel class. It calls the parent initializer, stores the configuration flags/values (bi, input_dim, gru_units, dense_units) and constructs the Keras layers used by the model: an initial dense layer (hidden1) of size dense_units, an intermediate dense (out) of size gru_units with tanh activation, two stacked GRU layers (gru_1 and gru_2) whose shapes depend on the bi (bidirectional) flag — if bi is True each GRU is wrapped in a Bidirectional layer; gru_1 returns sequences and state and uses gru_units units, gru_2 returns sequences and uses int(gru_units/2) units; GRU activations are 'elu'. Finally a TimeDistributed Dense output layer producing a single sigmoid value per time step is created. The initializer only builds and assigns these layers (does not compile the model). Default parameters: bi=False, input_dim=14, gru_units=128, dense_units=64.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70b701613085407db97b5deace4233ed</data>
      <data key="d4">custom_kg</data>
      <data key="d5">1759701943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="rnn_model::RNNModel::from_config">
      <data key="d0">rnn_model::RNNModel::from_config</data>
      <data key="d1">functions</data>
      <data key="d2">A simple constructor helper that creates and returns a new RNNModel instance from a configuration mapping. It calls the class constructor with the contents of the config dictionary unpacked as keyword arguments (equivalent to cls(**config)). The config is expected to supply the model's init parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-70b701613085407db97b5deace4233ed</data>
